WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-

2
00:07:38.458 --> 00:07:41.628
While I'm very familiar
with you and your family.

3
00:07:41.712 --> 00:07:45.382
I have no way of knowing 
if you are familiar with who I am.

4
00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:48.552
Are you aware of my existence?

5
00:07:49.553 --> 00:07:50.554
Yes.

6
00:07:50.637 --> 00:07:51.722
This is good.

7
00:07:52.306 --> 00:07:56.393
Now. are you aware of the job 
I've been ordered to carry out in France?

8
00:07:58.729 --> 00:07:59.771
Yes.

9
00:08:00.439 --> 00:08:02.441
Please tell me what you've heard.

10
00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:04.735
I've heard...

11
00:08:05.277 --> 00:08:09.573
that the Führer has put you in charge
of rounding up the Jews left in France

12
00:08:09.656 --> 00:08:12.576
who are either hiding
or passing for Gentile.

13
00:08:14.036 --> 00:08:16.914
The Führer couldn't have 
said it better himself.

14
00:08:18.874 --> 00:08:22.503
But the meaning of your visit.

15
00:08:22.961 --> 00:08:27.174
pleasant though it is.
is mysterious to me.

16
00:08:28.842 --> 00:08:32.095
The Germans looked through my house
nine months ago for hiding Jews

17
00:08:32.179 --> 00:08:33.847
and found nothing.

18
00:08:35.599 --> 00:08:37.267
I'm aware of that.

19
00:08:37.768 --> 00:08:40.270
I've read the reports of this area.

20
00:08:42.272 --> 00:08:45.484
But like any enterprise.
when under new management.

21
00:08:45.567 --> 00:08:48.654
there is always 
a slight duplication of efforts...

22
00:08:49.905 --> 00:08:54.576
most of it being a complete waste of time. 
but needs to be done nevertheless.

23
00:08:55.577 --> 00:08:58.622
I just have a few questions.
monsieur LaPadite.

24
00:09:00.123 --> 00:09:02.376
If you can assist me with answers.

25
00:09:02.459 --> 00:09:05.587
my department can close the file 
on your family.

26
00:09:14.054 --> 00:09:15.222
Now...

27
00:09:16.890 --> 00:09:21.144
before the occupation. 
there were four Jewish families in this area.

28
00:09:21.728 --> 00:09:24.064
all dairy farmers like yourself.

29
00:09:25.899 --> 00:09:30.487
Doleracs. Rollins. the Loveitts...

30
00:09:32.322 --> 00:09:33.991
and the Dreyfuses.

31
00:09:34.157 --> 00:09:35.701
Is that correct?

32
00:09:35.784 --> 00:09:36.785
To my knowledge.

33
00:09:36.869 --> 00:09:40.330
those were the Jewish families
among the dairy farmers.

34
00:09:40.497 --> 00:09:44.334
Herr Colonel. would it disturb you 
if I smoked my pipe?

35
00:09:44.418 --> 00:09:45.878
Please. monsieur LaPadite.

36
00:09:45.961 --> 00:09:48.964
this is your house.
make yourself comfortable.

37
00:09:49.298 --> 00:09:52.259
Now. according to these papers...

38
00:09:53.177 --> 00:09:56.597
all the Jewish families in this area 
have been accounted for

39
00:09:56.680 --> 00:09:59.516
except the Dreyfuses.

40
00:10:00.976 --> 00:10:04.396
Somewhere in the last year 
it would appear they've vanished.

41
00:10:04.479 --> 00:10:07.774
Which leads me to the conclusion that 
they've either made good their escape

42
00:10:07.858 --> 00:10:10.777
or someone is very successfully 
hiding them.

43
00:10:11.987 --> 00:10:15.616
What have you heard about  the Dreyfuses. 
monsieur LaPadite?

44
00:10:15.699 --> 00:10:16.658
Only rumors.

45
00:10:16.742 --> 00:10:18.035
I love rumors!

46
00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:20.954
Facts could be so misleading.

47
00:10:21.038 --> 00:10:24.208
where rumors. true or false. 
are often revealing.

48
00:10:24.625 --> 00:10:26.084
So. monsieur LaPadite.

49
00:10:26.168 --> 00:10:29.421
what rumors have you heard
regarding the Dreyfuses?

50
00:10:32.257 --> 00:10:35.385
Again. this is just a rumor.

51
00:10:35.469 --> 00:10:42.067
but we heard the Dreyfuses 
had made their way into Spain.

52
00:10:49.650 --> 00:10:52.361
So. the rumors you've heard
have been of escape?

53
00:10:54.071 --> 00:10:55.155
Yes.

54
00:10:58.742 --> 00:11:02.496
Having never met the Dreyfuses.
would you confirm for me

55
00:11:02.579 --> 00:11:05.874
the exact members of the household 
and their names?

56
00:11:11.296 --> 00:11:13.257
There were five of them.

57
00:11:15.467 --> 00:11:18.136
The father. Jacob.

58
00:11:20.013 --> 00:11:22.516
Wife. Miram.

59
00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:28.146
And her brother. Bob.

60
00:11:35.404 --> 00:11:36.947
How old is Bob?

61
00:11:38.574 --> 00:11:39.908
Thirty. 31.

62
00:11:44.163 --> 00:11:45.414
Continue.

63
00:11:45.789 --> 00:11:47.416
And the children...

64
00:11:49.126 --> 00:11:50.252
Amos...

65
00:11:52.337 --> 00:11:53.797
and Shosanna.

66
00:11:55.966 --> 00:11:57.801
Ages of the children?

67
00:12:04.892 --> 00:12:08.478
Amos was nine or 10.

68
00:12:11.315 --> 00:12:12.608
And Shosanna?

69
00:12:12.691 --> 00:12:14.818
And Shosanna was...

70
00:12:16.486 --> 00:12:20.282
18 or 19.
I'm not really sure.

71
00:12:31.126 --> 00:12:33.462
Well. I guess that should do it.

72
00:12:39.843 --> 00:12:44.264
However. before I go. could I have
another glass of your delicious milk?

73
00:12:47.309 --> 00:12:48.810
But of course.

74
00:12:55.567 --> 00:12:57.611
Monsieur LaPadite.

75
00:12:57.694 --> 00:13:01.698
are you aware of the nickname 
the people of France have given me?

76
00:13:05.327 --> 00:13:07.746
I have no interest in such things.

77
00:13:08.789 --> 00:13:11.500
But you are aware
of what they call me.

78
00:13:14.044 --> 00:13:15.379
I'm aware.

79
00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:19.007
What are you aware of?

80
00:13:28.892 --> 00:13:30.435
That they call you "The Jew Hunter."

81
00:13:30.519 --> 00:13:32.062
Precisely.

82
00:13:34.398 --> 00:13:37.025
I understand your trepidation 
in repeating it.

83
00:13:37.109 --> 00:13:39.403
Heydrich apparently hates the moniker

84
00:13:39.486 --> 00:13:42.155
the good people of Prague
have bestowed on him.

85
00:13:42.239 --> 00:13:45.492
Actually. why he would hate the name 
"the Hangman" is baffling to me.

86
00:13:45.576 --> 00:13:48.912
It would appear he has done
everything in his power to earn it.

87
00:13:48.996 --> 00:13:52.249
Now I. on the other hand.
love my unofficial title

88
00:13:52.332 --> 00:13:54.751
precisely because I've earned it.

89
00:13:56.170 --> 00:14:00.215
The feature that makes me such 
an effective hunter of the Jews is.

90
00:14:00.299 --> 00:14:03.010
as opposed to most German soldiers.

91
00:14:03.093 --> 00:14:05.095
I can think like a Jew

92
00:14:05.762 --> 00:14:08.473
where they can only think like a German.

93
00:14:08.849 --> 00:14:11.268
More precisely. a German soldier.

94
00:14:17.941 --> 00:14:22.905
Now. if one were to determine what attribute
the German people share with a beast...

95
00:14:23.447 --> 00:14:26.992
it would be the cunning 
and the predatory instinct of a hawk.

96
00:14:27.451 --> 00:14:31.288
But if one were to determine 
what attributes the Jews share with a beast.

97
00:14:31.371 --> 00:14:33.499
it would be that of the rat.

98
00:14:36.293 --> 00:14:40.130
The Führer and Goebbels' propaganda
have said pretty much the same thing.

99
00:14:40.214 --> 00:14:43.217
But where our conclusions differ.

100
00:14:43.300 --> 00:14:46.303
is I don't consider 
the comparison an insult.

101
00:14:48.805 --> 00:14:52.643
Consider for a moment 
the world a rat lives in.

102
00:14:53.560 --> 00:14:55.771
It's a hostile world. indeed.

103
00:14:56.605 --> 00:14:59.983
If a rat were to scamper through
your front door. right now.

104
00:15:00.067 --> 00:15:02.486
would you greet it with hostility?

105
00:15:03.487 --> 00:15:05.322
I suppose I would.

106
00:15:05.405 --> 00:15:06.949
Has a rat ever done anything to you

107
00:15:07.032 --> 00:15:10.327
to create this animosity
you feel toward them?

108
00:15:11.245 --> 00:15:13.872
Rats spread disease.
They bite people.

109
00:15:14.414 --> 00:15:18.210
Rats were the cause of the bubonic plague. 
but that's some time ago.

110
00:15:18.293 --> 00:15:20.921
I propose to you any disease
a rat could spread.

111
00:15:21.004 --> 00:15:23.465
a squirrel could equally carry.

112
00:15:23.549 --> 00:15:25.133
Would you agree?

113
00:15:27.010 --> 00:15:29.596
Yet. I assume you don't share
the same animosity with squirrels

114
00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:31.682
that you do with rats. do you?

115
00:15:31.765 --> 00:15:32.766
No.

116
00:15:32.850 --> 00:15:35.352
Yet. they're both rodents.
are they not?

117
00:15:35.435 --> 00:15:39.439
And except for the tail. 
they even rather look alike. don't they?

118
00:15:39.857 --> 00:15:42.693
It's an interesting thought.
Herr Colonel.

119
00:15:43.402 --> 00:15:45.445
However interesting
as the thought may be.

120
00:15:45.529 --> 00:15:48.782
it makes not one bit of difference 
to how you feel.

121
00:15:51.118 --> 00:15:55.205
If a rat were to walk in here. 
right now. as I'm talking...

122
00:15:56.331 --> 00:16:00.169
would you greet it with a saucer 
of your delicious milk?

123
00:16:00.252 --> 00:16:01.712
Probably not.

124
00:16:02.421 --> 00:16:04.089
I didn't think so.

125
00:16:04.715 --> 00:16:06.258
You don't like them.

126
00:16:06.341 --> 00:16:08.218
You don't really know
why you don't like them.

127
00:16:08.302 --> 00:16:11.054
All you know is you find them repulsive.

128
00:16:13.265 --> 00:16:16.310
Consequently. a German soldier 
conducts a search

129
00:16:16.393 --> 00:16:18.937
of a house suspected of hiding Jews.

130
00:16:19.855 --> 00:16:21.440
Where does the hawk look?

131
00:16:21.523 --> 00:16:24.693
He looks in the barn. he looks in the attic. 
he looks in the cellar.

132
00:16:24.776 --> 00:16:27.237
he looks everywhere he would hide.

133
00:16:28.197 --> 00:16:32.367
But there are so many places 
it would never occur to a hawk to hide.

134
00:16:34.620 --> 00:16:38.290
However. the reason the Führer has brought me 
off my Alps in Austria

135
00:16:38.373 --> 00:16:42.794
and placed me in French cow country today 
is because it does occur to me.

136
00:16:44.046 --> 00:16:47.382
Because I'm aware what tremendous feats 
human beings are capable of

137
00:16:47.466 --> 00:16:49.510
once they abandon dignity.

138
00:16:51.261 --> 00:16:53.430
May I smoke my pipe as well?

139
00:16:55.766 --> 00:16:58.644
Please. Herr Colonel.
make yourself at home.

140
00:17:11.406 --> 00:17:16.453
Now. my job dictates...

141
00:17:21.792 --> 00:17:24.461
that I must have my men
enter your home...

142
00:17:28.382 --> 00:17:30.259
and conduct a thorough search

143
00:17:30.342 --> 00:17:34.137
before I can officially cross
your family's name off my list.

144
00:17:34.888 --> 00:17:38.767
And if there are any irregularities
to be found. rest assured they will be.

145
00:17:38.851 --> 00:17:41.061
That is unless you have
something to tell me

146
00:17:41.144 --> 00:17:44.189
that makes the conducting
of a search unnecessary.

147
00:17:44.273 --> 00:17:46.525
I might add. also.
that any information

148
00:17:46.608 --> 00:17:51.280
that makes the performance of my duty easier 
will not be met with punishment.

149
00:17:52.114 --> 00:17:55.659
Actually. quite the contrary.
It will be met with reward.

150
00:17:56.160 --> 00:17:57.452
And that reward will be.

151
00:17:57.536 --> 00:18:00.330
your family will cease
to be harassed in any way

152
00:18:00.414 --> 00:18:04.835
by the German military during the rest 
of our occupation of your country.

153
00:18:15.512 --> 00:18:18.849
You're sheltering enemies
of the state. are you not?

154
00:18:24.188 --> 00:18:25.272
Yes.

155
00:18:28.192 --> 00:18:32.112
You're sheltering them underneath
your floorboards. aren't you?

156
00:18:34.656 --> 00:18:35.699
Yes.

157
00:18:38.535 --> 00:18:41.580
Point out to me the areas
where they're hiding.

158
00:19:02.601 --> 00:19:03.977
Since I haven't heard any disturbance.

159
00:19:04.061 --> 00:19:07.773
I assume. while they're listening.
they don't speak English.

160
00:19:09.691 --> 00:19:10.734
Yes.

161
00:19:12.819 --> 00:19:15.656
I'm going to switch back to French now.
and I want you to follow my masquerade.

162
00:19:15.739 --> 00:19:17.199
Is that clear?

163
00:19:19.159 --> 00:19:20.244
Yes.

164
00:20:22.181 --> 00:20:23.307
It's the girl.

165
00:21:09.561 --> 00:21:12.105
Au revoir. Shosanna!

166
00:21:27.538 --> 00:21:28.914
<i>Ten-hut!</i>

167
00:21:35.796 --> 00:21:37.673
My name is Lieutenant Aldo Raine.

168
00:21:37.756 --> 00:21:41.718
And I'm putting together a special team. 
and I need me eight soldiers.

169
00:21:41.802 --> 00:21:44.930
Eight Jewish American soldiers.

170
00:21:45.681 --> 00:21:49.476
Now. you all might've heard rumors
about the armada happening soon.

171
00:21:49.560 --> 00:21:52.271
Well. we'll be leaving a little earlier.

172
00:21:53.480 --> 00:21:56.775
We're going to be dropped into France 
dressed as civilians.

173
00:21:57.401 --> 00:21:59.695
Once we're in enemy territory...

174
00:22:00.320 --> 00:22:02.281
as a bushwhacking guerrilla army.

175
00:22:02.364 --> 00:22:05.742
we're going to be doing one thing 
and one thing only.

176
00:22:06.285 --> 00:22:07.744
Killing Nazis.

177
00:22:09.746 --> 00:22:11.331
I don't know about you all.

178
00:22:11.415 --> 00:22:14.334
but I sure as hell didn't come down
from the goddamn Smoky Mountains.

179
00:22:14.418 --> 00:22:18.338
cross 5.000 miles of water.
fight my way through half of Sicily

180
00:22:18.422 --> 00:22:22.843
and jump out of a fucking airplane 
to teach the Nazis lessons in humanity.

181
00:22:22.926 --> 00:22:25.012
Nazi ain't got no humanity.

182
00:22:25.762 --> 00:22:29.266
They're the foot soldiers of a Jew-hating. 
mass-murdering maniac

183
00:22:29.349 --> 00:22:31.602
and they need to be destroyed.

184
00:22:31.977 --> 00:22:36.315
That's why any and every son of a bitch 
we find wearing a Nazi uniform...

185
00:22:36.773 --> 00:22:38.609
they're going to die.

186
00:22:41.570 --> 00:22:44.990
Now. I'm the direct descendent
of the mountain man Jim Bridger. 

187
00:22:45.073 --> 00:22:47.201
That means I got
a little Indian in me.

188
00:22:47.284 --> 00:22:51.538
And our battle plan will be
that of an Apache resistance.

189
00:22:52.623 --> 00:22:54.958
We will be cruel to the Germans.

190
00:22:55.334 --> 00:22:58.629
And through our cruelty.
they will know who we are.

191
00:22:58.795 --> 00:23:01.048
And they will find
the evidence of our cruelty

192
00:23:01.131 --> 00:23:03.050
in the disemboweled. dismembered

193
00:23:03.133 --> 00:23:06.803
and disfigured bodies of their
brothers we leave behind us.

194
00:23:06.970 --> 00:23:09.389
And the German won't be able
to help themselves.

195
00:23:09.473 --> 00:23:13.227
but imagine the cruelty 
their brothers endured at our hands.

196
00:23:13.894 --> 00:23:17.314
and our boot heels
and the edge of our knives.

197
00:23:18.690 --> 00:23:21.068
And the German will be sickened by us.

198
00:23:21.151 --> 00:23:23.362
And the German will talk about us.

199
00:23:23.445 --> 00:23:25.656
And the German will fear us.

200
00:23:26.156 --> 00:23:28.659
And when the German
closes their eyes at night

201
00:23:28.742 --> 00:23:32.037
and they're tortured by their subconscious 
for the evil they have done.

202
00:23:32.120 --> 00:23:35.833
it will be with thoughts of us
that they are tortured with.

203
00:23:37.376 --> 00:23:38.544
Sound good?

204
00:23:38.627 --> 00:23:40.254
Yes. sir!

205
00:23:41.588 --> 00:23:43.382
That's what I like to hear.

206
00:23:43.590 --> 00:23:47.427
But I got a word of warning
for all you would-be warriors.

207
00:23:47.511 --> 00:23:50.389
When you join my command.
you take on debit.

208
00:23:50.806 --> 00:23:53.392
A debit you owe me. personally.

209
00:23:55.394 --> 00:23:59.982
Each and every man under my command 
owes me 100 Nazi scalps.

210
00:24:00.691 --> 00:24:02.526
And I want my scalps.

211
00:24:03.402 --> 00:24:08.615
And all y'all will get me 100 Nazi scalps
taken from the heads of 100 dead Nazis.

212
00:24:10.200 --> 00:24:12.119
Or you will die trying!

213
00:26:54.239 --> 00:26:55.908
Hey. Hirschberg.

214
00:26:56.658 --> 00:26:58.368
Send that Kraut sarge over.

215
00:26:58.452 --> 00:26:59.953
You. Go.

216
00:27:33.695 --> 00:27:35.739
Sergeant Werner Rachtman.

217
00:27:36.698 --> 00:27:39.243
Lieutenant Aldo Raine.
Pleased to meet you.

218
00:27:39.785 --> 00:27:41.829
You know what "sit down" means. Werner?

219
00:27:41.912 --> 00:27:43.705
- Yes.
- Then sit down. 

220
00:27:47.376 --> 00:27:48.460
How is your English. Werner?

221
00:27:48.544 --> 00:27:51.505
Because if need be. 
we got a couple of fellows who can translate.

222
00:27:51.588 --> 00:27:52.673
Wicki here.

223
00:27:52.756 --> 00:27:56.009
an Austrian-Jew. got the fuck out of Munich 
while the getting was good.

224
00:27:56.093 --> 00:28:00.013
Became American. got drafted.
come back to give y'all what for.

225
00:28:00.556 --> 00:28:03.183
Another one up there
you might be familiar with.

226
00:28:03.267 --> 00:28:05.185
Sergeant Hugo Stiglitz.

227
00:28:07.271 --> 00:28:08.772
Heard of him?

228
00:28:09.106 --> 00:28:12.776
Everybody in the German Army
has heard of Hugo Stiglitz.

229
00:28:23.453 --> 00:28:25.414
<i>The reason for Hugo Stiglitz's celebrity</i>

230
00:28:25.497 --> 00:28:27.624
<i>among German soldiers is simple.</i>

231
00:28:27.708 --> 00:28:33.380
<i>As a German-enlisted man.
he killed 13 Gestapo officers.</i>

232
00:28:47.644 --> 00:28:50.647
<i>Instead of putting him up
against a wall.</i>

233
00:28:50.731 --> 00:28:53.567
<i>the High Command decided
to send him back to Berlin</i>

234
00:28:53.650 --> 00:28:55.152
<i>to be made an example of.</i>

235
00:28:56.695 --> 00:29:00.449
<i>Needless to say. 
once the Basterds heard about him.</i>

236
00:29:00.782 --> 00:29:02.451
<i>he never got there.</i>

237
00:29:39.363 --> 00:29:41.240
Sergeant Hugo Stiglitz?

238
00:29:43.909 --> 00:29:46.620
Lieutenant Aldo Raine.
These are the Basterds.

239
00:29:46.703 --> 00:29:48.372
Ever heard of us?

240
00:29:50.374 --> 00:29:52.960
We just want to say 
we're a big fan of your work.

241
00:29:53.043 --> 00:29:54.169
When it comes to killing Nazis...

242
00:29:57.422 --> 00:29:59.675
I think you show great talent.

243
00:29:59.758 --> 00:30:03.554
And I pride myself for having an eye 
for that kind of talent.

244
00:30:07.057 --> 00:30:10.227
But your status as a Nazi killer 
is still amateur.

245
00:30:11.311 --> 00:30:14.314
We all come here to see
if you want to go pro.

246
00:30:21.155 --> 00:30:23.448
Can I assume you know who we are?

247
00:30:23.532 --> 00:30:24.867
You're Aldo the Apache.

248
00:30:27.286 --> 00:30:28.704
Werner. if you heard of us.

249
00:30:28.787 --> 00:30:31.456
you probably heard we ain't in
the prisoner-taking business.

250
00:30:31.540 --> 00:30:35.460
We in the killing Nazi business.
and. cousin. business is a-booming.

251
00:30:35.544 --> 00:30:36.837
Oh. yeah.

252
00:30:37.421 --> 00:30:39.965
Now. that leaves two ways
we can play this out.

253
00:30:40.048 --> 00:30:42.259
Either kill you or let you go.

254
00:30:42.801 --> 00:30:44.887
Whether or not you're going
to leave this ditch alive

255
00:30:44.970 --> 00:30:46.930
depends entirely on you.

256
00:30:51.268 --> 00:30:54.021
Up the road a piece.
there's an orchard.

257
00:30:54.438 --> 00:30:58.859
Besides you. we know there's another
Kraut patrol fucking around here somewhere.

258
00:30:59.735 --> 00:31:01.862
If that patrol were to have 
any crack shots.

259
00:31:01.945 --> 00:31:04.907
that orchard would be
a goddamn sniper's delight.

260
00:31:06.116 --> 00:31:09.453
So if you ever want to eat
a sauerkraut sandwich again...

261
00:31:10.871 --> 00:31:14.374
you got to show me on this here map 
where they are.

262
00:31:15.250 --> 00:31:18.587
You got to tell me how many they are. 
and you got to tell me

263
00:31:18.670 --> 00:31:21.131
what kind of artillery
they're carrying with them.

264
00:31:22.633 --> 00:31:26.845
You can't expect me to divulge information
that would put German lives in danger.

265
00:31:27.888 --> 00:31:31.892
Well. now. Werner. that's where you're wrong. 
because that's exactly what I expect.

266
00:31:32.643 --> 00:31:34.853
I need to know about
Germans hiding in trees.

267
00:31:34.937 --> 00:31:38.106
And you need to tell me. 
And you need to tell me right now.

268
00:31:39.316 --> 00:31:40.817
Now. just take that finger of yours

269
00:31:40.901 --> 00:31:44.238
and point out on this here map
where this party is being held.

270
00:31:44.321 --> 00:31:47.699
how many is coming 
and what they brought to play with.

271
00:31:54.832 --> 00:31:57.084
I respectfully refuse. sir.

272
00:31:59.419 --> 00:32:00.754
Hear that?

273
00:32:02.047 --> 00:32:03.131
Yes.

274
00:32:06.260 --> 00:32:08.554
That's Sergeant Donny Donowitz.

275
00:32:08.846 --> 00:32:11.557
You might know him better by his nickname.

276
00:32:11.640 --> 00:32:13.392
The Bear Jew.

277
00:32:14.476 --> 00:32:18.480
Now. if you heard of Aldo the Apache.
you got to have heard about The Bear Jew.

278
00:32:18.564 --> 00:32:19.815
I heard of The Bear Jew.

279
00:32:19.898 --> 00:32:21.525
What did you hear?

280
00:32:22.609 --> 00:32:25.028
Beats German soldiers with a club.

281
00:32:25.487 --> 00:32:29.199
He bashes their brains in 
with a baseball bat. what he does.

282
00:32:29.533 --> 00:32:31.618
And. Werner. I'm going to ask you 
one last goddamn time.

283
00:32:31.702 --> 00:32:33.579
and if you still respectfully refuse.

284
00:32:33.662 --> 00:32:35.706
I'm calling The Bear Jew over.

285
00:32:35.789 --> 00:32:37.708
He's going to take
that big bat of his.

286
00:32:37.791 --> 00:32:40.961
and he's going to beat your ass 
to death with it.

287
00:32:44.256 --> 00:32:46.091
Now. take your
Wiener-schnitzel-licking finger.

288
00:32:46.175 --> 00:32:49.178
and point out on this map
what I want to know.

289
00:32:57.269 --> 00:32:58.562
Fuck you.

290
00:32:59.021 --> 00:33:00.647
And your Jew dogs.

291
00:33:04.610 --> 00:33:06.570
Actually. Werner. we're all tickled 
to hear you say that.

292
00:33:06.653 --> 00:33:08.530
Quite frankly. 
watching Donny beat Nazis to death

293
00:33:08.614 --> 00:33:11.492
is the closest we ever get
to going to the movies. Donny!

294
00:33:11.575 --> 00:33:12.701
Yeah?

295
00:33:12.784 --> 00:33:15.329
Got us a German here 
who wants to die for country.

296
00:33:15.412 --> 00:33:16.747
Oblige him.

297
00:34:23.313 --> 00:34:25.816
Did you get that for killing Jews?

298
00:34:25.983 --> 00:34:27.276
Bravery.

299
00:34:43.834 --> 00:34:44.960
Yeah!

300
00:34:47.588 --> 00:34:49.923
Oh. no!
Oh. no!

301
00:34:50.007 --> 00:34:51.175
Donny!

302
00:34:51.758 --> 00:34:52.926
Yeah. Donny!

303
00:34:53.177 --> 00:34:55.929
About now I'd be shitting my pants 
if I was you.

304
00:34:57.431 --> 00:35:00.100
Teddy Fucking Williams
knocks it out of the park!

305
00:35:00.184 --> 00:35:03.770
Fenway Park is on its feet
for Teddy Fucking Ballgame!

306
00:35:03.854 --> 00:35:07.774
He went yard on that one.
on to fucking Lansdowne Street!

307
00:35:07.858 --> 00:35:08.942
You!

308
00:35:12.112 --> 00:35:13.864
Damn it. Hirschberg!

309
00:35:13.947 --> 00:35:16.867
Donny. bring that other one 
over here. Alive!

310
00:35:17.159 --> 00:35:20.078
Get the fuck up! 
Batter up. You're on deck!

311
00:35:20.370 --> 00:35:23.081
Two hits. 
I hit you. you hit the ground.

312
00:35:24.124 --> 00:35:25.292
English?

313
00:35:26.418 --> 00:35:27.586
Wicki.

314
00:35:31.215 --> 00:35:33.175
Ask him if he wants to live.

315
00:35:35.469 --> 00:35:37.721
Tell him to point out on this map 
the German position.

316
00:35:42.643 --> 00:35:44.269
Ask him how many Germans.

317
00:35:46.730 --> 00:35:48.357
Around about 12.

318
00:35:48.524 --> 00:35:49.900
What kind of artillery?

319
00:36:01.662 --> 00:36:03.247
Now. when you report
what happened here.

320
00:36:03.330 --> 00:36:07.000
you can't tell them you told us
what you told us. They'll shoot you.

321
00:36:07.084 --> 00:36:11.004
They're going to want to know 
why you so special. we let you live.

322
00:36:11.088 --> 00:36:14.758
So tell them. we let you live so you
could spread the word through the ranks

323
00:36:14.842 --> 00:36:17.302
what's going to happen
to every Nazi we find.

324
00:36:39.867 --> 00:36:43.120
Now that you've survived the war. 
when you get home. what you going to do?

325
00:36:49.251 --> 00:36:51.461
He's going to hug his mother.

326
00:36:53.630 --> 00:36:55.382
Well. ain't that nice?

327
00:36:55.591 --> 00:36:57.301
Ask if he's going
to take off his uniform.

328
00:37:02.389 --> 00:37:04.266
He's going to burn it.

329
00:37:04.558 --> 00:37:07.269
Yeah. that's what we thought. 
We don't like that.

330
00:37:08.312 --> 00:37:12.232
See. we like our Nazis in uniforms.
That way you can spot them.

331
00:37:12.316 --> 00:37:13.859
Just like that.

332
00:37:18.489 --> 00:37:22.743
But you take off that uniform. 
ain't nobody going to know you's a Nazi.

333
00:37:22.826 --> 00:37:24.995
And that don't sit well with us.

334
00:37:30.167 --> 00:37:33.670
So I'm going to give you 
a little something you can't take off.

335
00:37:45.849 --> 00:37:49.520
You know. Lieutenant. 
you're getting pretty good at that.

336
00:37:49.978 --> 00:37:53.148
You know how you get to Carnegie Hall. 
don't you?

337
00:37:54.107 --> 00:37:55.359
Practice.

338
00:54:17.966 --> 00:54:20.302
Au revoir. Shosanna!

339
01:02:34.713 --> 01:02:39.092
<i>At that time. 35 millimeter nitrate film 
was so flammable</i>

340
01:02:39.176 --> 01:02:42.221
<i>that you couldn't even
bring a reel onto a streetcar.</i>

341
01:02:42.429 --> 01:02:44.139
<i>Hey. you can't bring those here 
on a public vehicle.</i>

342
01:02:44.223 --> 01:02:45.641
<i>- They're films. ain't they? 
- Yes.</i> 

343
01:02:45.724 --> 01:02:47.392
<i>Then they're flammable.
Go on. hop off.</i>

344
01:02:47.559 --> 01:02:51.396
<i>Because nitrate film burns
three times faster than paper.</i>

345
01:02:55.025 --> 01:02:57.069
<i>Shosanna has a collection</i>

346
01:02:57.152 --> 01:03:02.199
<i>of over 350 nitrate film prints.</i>

347
01:04:13.770 --> 01:04:15.939
Right this way. Lieutenant.

348
01:04:36.126 --> 01:04:38.795
Lieutenant Archie Hicox reporting. sir.

349
01:04:38.879 --> 01:04:41.673
General Ed Fenech. 
At ease. Hicox. 

350
01:04:42.508 --> 01:04:43.717
Drink?

351
01:04:45.469 --> 01:04:49.681
If you offer me a scotch and plain water.
I could drink a scotch and plain water.

352
01:04:49.765 --> 01:04:53.352
That-a-boy. Lieutenant. 
Make it yourself like a good chap. will you?

353
01:04:53.435 --> 01:04:55.437
The bar is in the globe.

354
01:04:59.817 --> 01:05:01.902
Something for yourself. sir?

355
01:05:01.985 --> 01:05:05.155
Whiskey. Straight.
No junk in it.

356
01:05:06.406 --> 01:05:09.326
It says here that
you speak German fluently.

357
01:05:09.409 --> 01:05:11.370
Like a Katzenjammer Kid.

358
01:05:11.453 --> 01:05:14.081
And your occupation before the war?

359
01:05:14.164 --> 01:05:15.332
I'm a film critic.

360
01:05:15.958 --> 01:05:17.918
List your accomplishments.

361
01:05:18.001 --> 01:05:19.878
Well. sir. such as they are.

362
01:05:19.962 --> 01:05:24.508
I write reviews and articles 
for a publication called Films and Filmmakers.

363
01:05:24.591 --> 01:05:27.010
and I've had two books published.

364
01:05:27.344 --> 01:05:30.931
Impressive. Don't be modest. Lieutenant. 
What are their titles?

365
01:05:31.014 --> 01:05:32.015
The first book was called

366
01:05:32.099 --> 01:05:36.603
Art of the Eyes. the Heart and the Mind:
A Study of German Cinema in the '20s.

367
01:05:36.687 --> 01:05:40.524
And the second one was called
Twenty-Four Frame da Vinci.

368
01:05:40.607 --> 01:05:45.946
It's a subtextual film criticism study
of the work of German director G.W. Pabst.

369
01:05:46.446 --> 01:05:48.031
What should we drink to. sir?

370
01:05:48.115 --> 01:05:49.366
Well...

371
01:05:50.617 --> 01:05:52.578
Down with Hitler.

372
01:05:52.661 --> 01:05:54.037
All the way down. sir.

373
01:05:54.413 --> 01:05:55.664
Yes.

374
01:05:59.376 --> 01:06:03.463
Are you familiar with German cinema 
under the Third Reich?

375
01:06:05.340 --> 01:06:09.553
Yes. Obviously. I haven't seen any of the films 
made in the last three years.

376
01:06:09.636 --> 01:06:11.889
but I'm familiar with it.

377
01:06:11.972 --> 01:06:13.015
Explain it to me.

378
01:06:13.682 --> 01:06:14.725
Pardon. sir?

379
01:06:14.808 --> 01:06:19.062
Well. this little escapade of ours 
requires a knowledge of the German film industry

380
01:06:19.146 --> 01:06:24.318
under the Third Reich. 
Explain to me UFA under Goebbels.

381
01:06:26.487 --> 01:06:28.864
Goebbels considers the films he's making

382
01:06:28.947 --> 01:06:32.201
to be the beginning 
of a new era in German cinema.

383
01:06:32.659 --> 01:06:34.328
An alternative to what he considers

384
01:06:34.411 --> 01:06:37.372
the Jewish-German intellectual cinema 
of the '20s...

385
01:06:38.081 --> 01:06:40.751
and the Jewish-controlled dogma 
of Hollywood.

386
01:06:40.834 --> 01:06:42.419
How's he doing?

387
01:06:42.961 --> 01:06:45.547
Frightfully sorry. sir.
Once again? 

388
01:06:46.006 --> 01:06:50.594
You say he wants to take on the Jews 
at their own game.

389
01:06:51.595 --> 01:06:54.598
Well. compared to. say. 
Louis B. Mayer...

390
01:06:55.432 --> 01:06:57.684
how's he doing?

391
01:06:57.768 --> 01:06:59.019
Quite well. actually.

392
01:06:59.686 --> 01:07:01.271
Since Goebbels has taken over.

393
01:07:01.355 --> 01:07:05.776
film attendance has steadily risen in Germany 
over the last eight years.

394
01:07:05.859 --> 01:07:09.321
But Louis B. Mayer wouldn't be
Goebbels' proper opposite number.

395
01:07:09.404 --> 01:07:13.200
I believe Goebbels sees himself closer 
to David O. Selznick.

396
01:07:17.621 --> 01:07:18.997
Brief him.

397
01:07:19.331 --> 01:07:24.378
Lieutenant Hicox. at this point and time
I'd like to brief you on Operation Kino.

398
01:07:24.962 --> 01:07:26.088
Three days from now

399
01:07:26.171 --> 01:07:30.509
Joseph Goebbels is throwing a gala premiere 
of one of his new movies in Paris.

400
01:07:30.634 --> 01:07:31.718
What film. sir?

401
01:07:31.802 --> 01:07:34.471
The motion picture is called 
Nation's Pride.

402
01:07:35.430 --> 01:07:38.809
In attendance at this 
joyous Germatic occasion

403
01:07:38.892 --> 01:07:43.313
will be Goebbels. Goring. Bormann.
and most of the German High Command

404
01:07:43.397 --> 01:07:47.151
including all high ranking officers
of both the SS and the Gestapo.

405
01:07:47.234 --> 01:07:50.654
as well as luminaries of the
Nazi propaganda film industry.

406
01:07:50.737 --> 01:07:52.823
The master race at play?

407
01:07:52.906 --> 01:07:57.077
Basically. we have all our rotten eggs 
in one basket.

408
01:07:57.161 --> 01:07:59.705
The objective of Operation Kino...

409
01:08:00.622 --> 01:08:02.374
blow up the basket.

410
01:08:03.167 --> 01:08:07.254
And like the snows of yesteryear. 
gone from this earth.

411
01:08:08.172 --> 01:08:09.840
Jolly good. sir.

412
01:08:10.591 --> 01:08:14.094
An American Secret Service outfit
that lives deep behind enemy lines

413
01:08:14.178 --> 01:08:15.721
will be your assist.

414
01:08:15.804 --> 01:08:19.683
The Germans call them the Basterds.

415
01:08:20.225 --> 01:08:23.437
The Basterds.
Never heard of them.

416
01:08:23.604 --> 01:08:26.440
Whole point of the Secret Service.
old boy. you not hearing of them.

417
01:08:26.523 --> 01:08:30.527
But the Jerries have heard of them. 
because these Yanks have been them the devil.

418
01:08:30.611 --> 01:08:35.324
You'll be dropped into France.
about 24 kilometers outside of Paris.

419
01:08:35.407 --> 01:08:37.493
The Basterds will be waiting for you.

420
01:08:37.576 --> 01:08:40.329
First thing. you'll go to 
a little village called Nadine.

421
01:08:41.455 --> 01:08:44.249
In Nadine. there's a tavern 
called La Louisiane.

422
01:08:44.333 --> 01:08:47.503
There you'll rendezvous with our double agent. 
She'll take it from there.

423
01:08:47.586 --> 01:08:49.713
She's the one who is going
to get you into the premiere.

424
01:08:49.796 --> 01:08:53.550
It'll be you. her. and two
German-born members of the Basterds.

425
01:08:53.634 --> 01:08:57.054
She's also made all the other arrangements 
you're going to need.

426
01:08:57.888 --> 01:08:59.056
How will I know her?

427
01:08:59.181 --> 01:09:02.392
I suspect that won't be
too much trouble for you.

428
01:09:03.477 --> 01:09:06.396
Your contact is Bridget von Hammersmark.

429
01:09:06.480 --> 01:09:07.940
Bridget von Hammersmark?

430
01:09:09.191 --> 01:09:12.194
The German movie star
is working for England?

431
01:09:12.277 --> 01:09:14.863
Yes. for the last two years now.

432
01:09:14.947 --> 01:09:18.492
One could even say that
Operation Kino was her brainchild.

433
01:09:18.575 --> 01:09:19.743
Indeed.

434
01:09:19.827 --> 01:09:20.869
Got the gist?

435
01:09:20.953 --> 01:09:23.705
I think so. sir.
Paris when it sizzles. 

436
01:09:27.835 --> 01:09:31.338
You didn't say the goddamn rendezvous 
is in a fucking basement.

437
01:09:31.421 --> 01:09:32.756
I didn't know.

438
01:09:32.840 --> 01:09:34.258
You said it was in a tavern.

439
01:09:34.341 --> 01:09:35.509
It is a tavern.

440
01:09:35.592 --> 01:09:36.969
Yeah. in a basement.

441
01:09:37.636 --> 01:09:40.514
You know. fighting in a basement
offers a lot of difficulties.

442
01:09:40.597 --> 01:09:43.892
Number one being. 
you're fighting in a basement.

443
01:09:43.976 --> 01:09:45.853
What if we go in there
and she's not even there?

444
01:09:45.936 --> 01:09:47.187
We wait.

445
01:09:48.021 --> 01:09:52.109
Don't worry. She's a British spy. 
She'll make the rendezvous.

446
01:10:13.630 --> 01:10:15.966
Stiglitz. right?

447
01:10:16.049 --> 01:10:17.092
That's right. sir.

448
01:10:18.343 --> 01:10:20.846
I hear you're pretty good with that.

449
01:10:24.641 --> 01:10:27.769
You know. we're not looking
for trouble right now.

450
01:10:28.020 --> 01:10:31.565
Simply making contact with our agent. 
Should be uneventful.

451
01:10:33.400 --> 01:10:38.280
However. the off chance I'm wrong. 
things prove eventful...

452
01:10:39.490 --> 01:10:42.409
I need to know we can all remain calm.

453
01:10:47.122 --> 01:10:48.540
I don't look calm to you?

454
01:10:51.502 --> 01:10:56.381
Well. now that you put it like that. 
I guess you do.

455
01:11:11.522 --> 01:11:17.319
This Jerry of yours. Stiglitz. 
not exactly the loquacious type. is he?

456
01:11:19.154 --> 01:11:22.866
Is that the kind of man you need? 
Loquacious type?

457
01:11:24.618 --> 01:11:27.162
Fair point. Lieutenant.

458
01:11:29.456 --> 01:11:32.209
So you all get in trouble in there. 
what are we supposed to do?

459
01:11:32.292 --> 01:11:34.503
Make bets on how it all comes out?

460
01:11:35.712 --> 01:11:38.882
If we get into trouble.
we can handle it.

461
01:11:40.384 --> 01:11:43.303
But if trouble does happen.
we need you to make damn sure

462
01:11:43.387 --> 01:11:47.558
no Germans. or French. for that matter. 
escape from that basement.

463
01:11:48.475 --> 01:11:52.729
If Frau von Hammersmark's cover is compromised. 
the mission is kaput.

464
01:11:53.063 --> 01:11:58.735
Speaking of Frau von Hammersmark. 
whose idea was it for the deathtrap rendezvous?

465
01:11:59.736 --> 01:12:01.155
She chose the spot.

466
01:12:01.238 --> 01:12:02.865
Isn't that just dandy?

467
01:12:02.948 --> 01:12:06.910
Look. she's not a military strategist. 
She's just an actress.

468
01:12:07.286 --> 01:12:11.123
You don't got to be Stonewall Jackson 
to know you don't want to fight in a basement.

469
01:12:11.206 --> 01:12:13.250
She wasn't picking a place to fight.

470
01:12:13.333 --> 01:12:16.128
She was picking a place isolated 
and without Germans.

471
01:15:23.357 --> 01:15:24.358
Mmm.

472
01:31:45.589 --> 01:31:47.925
Well. if this is it. old boy...

473
01:31:48.509 --> 01:31:51.512
I hope you don't mind 
if I go out speaking the King's.

474
01:31:52.638 --> 01:31:54.556
By all means. Captain.

475
01:32:00.604 --> 01:32:04.233
There's a special rung in hell 
reserved for people who waste good Scotch.

476
01:32:05.651 --> 01:32:08.445
Seeing as I may be rapping
on the door momentarily...

477
01:32:13.534 --> 01:32:17.162
I must say. damn good stuff. sir.

478
01:32:20.457 --> 01:32:23.293
Now. about this pickle...

479
01:32:24.878 --> 01:32:26.672
we find ourselves in.

480
01:32:29.091 --> 01:32:32.177
It would appear there's only
one thing left for you to do.

481
01:32:32.261 --> 01:32:34.138
And what would that be?

482
01:32:34.847 --> 01:32:35.848
Stiglitz.

483
01:32:35.931 --> 01:32:37.349
Say auf Wiedersehen to your Nazi balls.

484
01:33:14.094 --> 01:33:15.846
You outside.
Who are you? 

485
01:33:16.430 --> 01:33:18.098
British? American?

486
01:33:18.849 --> 01:33:19.975
What?

487
01:33:20.767 --> 01:33:22.311
We're American.

488
01:33:22.603 --> 01:33:24.062
What are you?

489
01:33:24.396 --> 01:33:26.356
I'm a German. you idiot.

490
01:33:26.690 --> 01:33:29.401
Speak English pretty good for a German.

491
01:33:29.485 --> 01:33:30.694
I agree.

492
01:33:31.987 --> 01:33:33.489
So let's talk.

493
01:33:34.239 --> 01:33:35.616
Okay. talk.

494
01:33:36.325 --> 01:33:37.784
I'm a father.

495
01:33:39.036 --> 01:33:41.955
My baby was born today.
In Frankfurt.

496
01:33:42.456 --> 01:33:43.999
Five hours ago.

497
01:33:44.625 --> 01:33:48.879
His name is Max. 
We were in here drinking. celebrating.

498
01:33:49.713 --> 01:33:53.133
They're the ones that came in shooting and killing. 
It's not my fault!

499
01:33:53.217 --> 01:33:55.344
Okay!
It wasn't your fault.

500
01:33:56.720 --> 01:33:58.514
What's your name. soldier?

501
01:33:58.597 --> 01:33:59.848
Wilhelm.

502
01:34:00.724 --> 01:34:04.269
Now. is there anybody alive on our side?

503
01:34:04.353 --> 01:34:06.146
- No.
- I'm alive! 

504
01:34:08.357 --> 01:34:09.733
Who's that?

505
01:34:12.528 --> 01:34:14.530
Is the girl on your side?

506
01:34:16.073 --> 01:34:17.324
Which girl?

507
01:34:17.407 --> 01:34:19.827
Who do you think?
Von Hammersmark. 

508
01:34:21.411 --> 01:34:23.038
Yeah. she's ours.

509
01:34:23.872 --> 01:34:25.123
Is she okay?

510
01:34:28.126 --> 01:34:29.169
Wilhelm!

511
01:34:30.420 --> 01:34:32.047
She's been shot.

512
01:34:33.048 --> 01:34:34.633
But she's alive.

513
01:34:38.554 --> 01:34:40.055
Okay. Wilhelm.

514
01:34:41.056 --> 01:34:43.475
What do you say we make us a deal?

515
01:34:44.810 --> 01:34:46.186
What's your name?

516
01:34:46.270 --> 01:34:47.396
Aldo.

517
01:34:48.272 --> 01:34:50.524
Okay. Wilhelm. here's my deal.

518
01:34:50.774 --> 01:34:54.403
You let me and one of my men come down there 
and take the girl away.

519
01:34:54.486 --> 01:34:57.030
No guns. 
No guns me. no guns you.

520
01:34:57.114 --> 01:35:00.659
And we take the girl and leave. 
It's that simple. Willi.

521
01:35:01.034 --> 01:35:03.495
You go your way. we go ours.

522
01:35:03.579 --> 01:35:06.456
And little Max gets to grow up
playing catch with his daddy.

523
01:35:07.624 --> 01:35:10.544
So what do you say. Willi?
We got us a deal?

524
01:35:14.965 --> 01:35:16.049
Aldo...

525
01:35:17.301 --> 01:35:18.927
I'm here. Willi.

526
01:35:20.554 --> 01:35:22.306
I want to trust you.

527
01:35:22.389 --> 01:35:23.557
But...

528
01:35:24.475 --> 01:35:25.976
But how can I?

529
01:35:28.187 --> 01:35:30.189
What choice you got. son?

530
01:35:36.069 --> 01:35:38.113
Okay. okay.

531
01:35:39.698 --> 01:35:40.908
Aldo...

532
01:35:41.992 --> 01:35:43.619
I'm going to trust you.

533
01:35:44.495 --> 01:35:45.496
Come down.

534
01:36:01.470 --> 01:36:04.431
Hey. Willi. what's with the machine gun? 
I thought we had us a deal?

535
01:36:04.515 --> 01:36:06.767
We still have a deal.
Now. get the girl and go.

536
01:36:06.850 --> 01:36:08.393
Not so fast.

537
01:36:08.477 --> 01:36:11.063
We only got a deal.
we trust each other.

538
01:36:11.146 --> 01:36:12.856
And a Mexican standoff ain't trust.

539
01:36:13.357 --> 01:36:15.859
You need guns on me for it
to be a Mexican standoff.

540
01:36:16.527 --> 01:36:19.655
You got guns on us. 
You decide to shoot. we're dead.

541
01:36:19.738 --> 01:36:23.033
Up top. they got grenades. 
They drop them down here. you're dead.

542
01:36:23.116 --> 01:36:25.494
That's a Mexican standoff.
and that was not the deal.

543
01:36:25.577 --> 01:36:27.246
No trust. no deal.

544
01:36:43.137 --> 01:36:44.721
All right. Aldo.

545
01:36:46.390 --> 01:36:47.516
Fine.

546
01:36:50.894 --> 01:36:54.314
Just take that fucking traitor.
and get her out of my sight.

547
01:37:06.410 --> 01:37:09.830
Not so goddamn fast. doc. 
Tell him to go play with his dogs.

548
01:37:22.009 --> 01:37:25.929
Before we yank that slug out you.
you need to answer a few questions.

549
01:37:26.013 --> 01:37:27.806
Few questions about what?

550
01:37:28.307 --> 01:37:30.476
About I got three men dead back there.

551
01:37:30.559 --> 01:37:33.353
Why don't you try telling us
what the fuck happened?

552
01:37:33.437 --> 01:37:37.399
The British officer blew his German act 
and the Gestapo major saw it.

553
01:37:38.484 --> 01:37:40.736
Before we get into who shot John...

554
01:37:41.570 --> 01:37:45.699
why'd you invite my men to a rendezvous
in a basement with a bunch of Nazis?

555
01:37:50.621 --> 01:37:53.040
I can see since you didn't see 
what happened inside.

556
01:37:53.123 --> 01:37:55.793
that the Nazis being there
must look odd.

557
01:37:55.876 --> 01:37:58.378
Yeah. we got a word 
for that kind of odd in English.

558
01:37:58.462 --> 01:38:00.464
It's called suspicious.

559
01:38:04.760 --> 01:38:06.553
Everybody needs to calm down.

560
01:38:06.637 --> 01:38:09.306
You're letting your imagination
get the better of you.

561
01:38:10.682 --> 01:38:13.644
You met the sergeant yourself. Willi.

562
01:38:13.727 --> 01:38:15.562
You remember him. don't you?

563
01:38:15.646 --> 01:38:16.647
Yeah. I remember him.

564
01:38:16.730 --> 01:38:20.484
His wife had a baby tonight.
He had just become a...

565
01:38:20.567 --> 01:38:22.277
He had just become a father!

566
01:38:22.361 --> 01:38:26.198
His commanding officer gave him and his mates 
the night off to celebrate.

567
01:38:29.576 --> 01:38:35.633
The Germans being there was either a trap 
set by me or a tragic coincidence.

568
01:38:35.916 --> 01:38:37.668
It couldn't be both.

569
01:38:47.886 --> 01:38:49.763
How'd the shooting start?

570
01:38:49.847 --> 01:38:52.349
The Englishman gave himself away.

571
01:38:52.432 --> 01:38:54.059
How'd he do that?

572
01:38:55.310 --> 01:38:57.521
He ordered three glasses.

573
01:38:58.730 --> 01:39:00.649
We order three glasses.

574
01:39:00.858 --> 01:39:02.818
That's the German three.

575
01:39:03.694 --> 01:39:05.487
The other looks odd.

576
01:39:06.071 --> 01:39:08.407
Germans would and did notice it.

577
01:39:17.040 --> 01:39:19.126
Okay. let's pretend there were no Germans

578
01:39:19.209 --> 01:39:21.795
and everything went exactly
the way it was supposed to.

579
01:39:21.879 --> 01:39:23.797
What was the next step?

580
01:39:24.047 --> 01:39:25.257
Tuxedos.

581
01:39:25.924 --> 01:39:28.677
To get them into the premiere
wearing military uniforms

582
01:39:28.760 --> 01:39:31.555
with all the military there
would've been suicide.

583
01:39:33.557 --> 01:39:36.810
But going as members
of the German film industry...

584
01:39:37.227 --> 01:39:40.397
they wear tuxedos 
and fit in with everybody else.

585
01:39:41.899 --> 01:39:45.068
I arranged for the tailor
to fit three tuxedos tonight.

586
01:39:46.278 --> 01:39:48.697
How'd you intend to get them
in that premiere?

587
01:39:48.780 --> 01:39:50.407
Hand me my purse.

588
01:40:00.292 --> 01:40:02.711
Lieutenant Hicox was going as my escort.

589
01:40:04.046 --> 01:40:08.050
The other two were going 
as a German cameraman and his assistant.

590
01:40:09.176 --> 01:40:10.844
You still get us in that premiere?

591
01:40:10.928 --> 01:40:14.097
You speak German better 
than your friends? No. 

592
01:40:14.515 --> 01:40:16.725
Have I been shot? Yes! 

593
01:40:17.267 --> 01:40:22.105
I don't see me tripping the light fantastique 
up a red carpet anytime soon.

594
01:40:23.106 --> 01:40:25.526
Least of all. by tomorrow night.

595
01:40:38.413 --> 01:40:41.708
However. there's something
you don't know.

596
01:40:43.794 --> 01:40:47.881
There've been two recent developments 
regarding Operation Kino.

597
01:40:49.675 --> 01:40:54.763
One. the venue has been changed from The Ritz 
to a much smaller venue.

598
01:40:55.305 --> 01:40:58.475
Enormous change at the last minute? 
That's not very Germatic.

599
01:40:58.559 --> 01:41:01.520
Why the hell is Goebbels
doing stuff so damn peculiar?

600
01:41:01.603 --> 01:41:05.315
It probably has something to do 
with the second development.

601
01:41:05.691 --> 01:41:06.984
Which is?

602
01:41:11.280 --> 01:41:13.866
Der Führer is attending the premiere.

603
01:41:48.609 --> 01:41:50.235
Fuck a duck!

604
01:41:58.869 --> 01:42:00.746
What are you thinking?

605
01:42:02.039 --> 01:42:04.208
I'm thinking getting a whack
at planting old Uncle Adolf

606
01:42:04.291 --> 01:42:06.168
makes this horse a different color.

607
01:42:06.251 --> 01:42:07.920
What is that supposed to mean?

608
01:42:08.003 --> 01:42:09.922
It means you getting us
in that premiere.

609
01:42:10.005 --> 01:42:12.925
I'm probably going to end up 
losing this leg.

610
01:42:13.550 --> 01:42:15.928
Bye-bye. acting career.
Fun while it lasted.

611
01:42:16.011 --> 01:42:18.889
How do you expect me
to walk the red carpet?

612
01:42:21.058 --> 01:42:24.061
Doggy doc's going to dig that slug 
out your gam.

613
01:42:24.144 --> 01:42:26.188
He's going to wrap it up in a cast.

614
01:42:26.271 --> 01:42:28.398
and you got a good 
how-I-broke-my-leg-mountain-climbing story.

615
01:42:28.482 --> 01:42:31.151
That's German. ain't it? 
You all like climbing mountains. don't you?

616
01:42:31.235 --> 01:42:34.530
I don't. I like smoking. drinking
and ordering in restaurants.

617
01:42:34.613 --> 01:42:36.406
But I see your point.

618
01:42:36.657 --> 01:42:40.160
We fill you up with morphine
till it's coming out your ears

619
01:42:40.244 --> 01:42:43.539
and just limp your little ass 
up that reuge carpet.

620
01:42:45.040 --> 01:42:48.293
I know this is a silly question 
before I ask it.

621
01:42:48.377 --> 01:42:53.757
but can you Americans speak
any other language than English?

622
01:42:54.591 --> 01:42:56.844
We both speak a little Italian.

623
01:42:56.927 --> 01:42:59.429
With an atrocious accent. no doubt.

624
01:43:01.181 --> 01:43:04.643
But that doesn't exactly
kill us in the crib.

625
01:43:05.435 --> 01:43:08.272
Germans don't have a good ear for Italian.

626
01:43:12.192 --> 01:43:16.029
So you mumble Italian and brazen through it. 
Is that the plan?

627
01:43:16.280 --> 01:43:17.906
That's about it.

628
01:43:21.743 --> 01:43:22.744
That sounds good.

629
01:43:22.828 --> 01:43:25.205
It sounds like shit. 
What else are we going to do? Go home?

630
01:43:25.289 --> 01:43:27.124
No. that sounds good.

631
01:43:27.958 --> 01:43:31.879
If you don't blow it. with that.
I can get you in the building.

632
01:43:32.880 --> 01:43:33.922
Who does what?

633
01:43:34.006 --> 01:43:38.177
Well. I speak the most Italian. 
so I'll be your escort.

634
01:43:38.260 --> 01:43:41.388
Donowitz speaks second most. 
so he'll be your Italian cameraman.

635
01:43:41.472 --> 01:43:44.475
Omar. third most.
He'll be Donny's assistant.

636
01:43:45.017 --> 01:43:46.143
I don't speak Italian.

637
01:43:46.226 --> 01:43:49.605
Like I said. third best. 
Just keep your fucking mouth shut.

638
01:43:49.688 --> 01:43:51.231
In fact. why don't you 
start practicing right now?

639
01:47:20.607 --> 01:47:21.608
Yes.

640
01:53:50.873 --> 01:53:52.672
Gorlomi?

641
01:54:02.259 --> 01:54:08.140
Gorlomi.

642
01:54:12.644 --> 01:54:14.396
Gorlomi.

643
01:54:16.940 --> 01:54:18.775
Antonio Margheriti.

644
01:54:21.320 --> 01:54:23.037
Margheriti.

645
01:54:30.454 --> 01:54:31.789
Margheriti.

646
01:54:32.956 --> 01:54:33.957
Dominick Decocco.

647
01:54:34.082 --> 01:54:36.460
Dominick Decocco.

648
02:00:23.849 --> 02:00:25.642
What's that American expression?

649
02:00:25.726 --> 02:00:28.145
"If the shoe fits. you must wear it."

650
02:01:31.625 --> 02:01:36.213
Fucking shithead. Faggot fuck. 
Fuck you!

651
02:01:36.338 --> 02:01:38.340
Bunch of shithead fuck.

652
02:01:41.260 --> 02:01:42.803
Fuck you. too!

653
02:01:45.430 --> 02:01:49.560
Goddamn Nazi farts. sons of bitches! 
Get your hands off me.

654
02:01:50.060 --> 02:01:53.564
You fucking bratwurst-smelling...
Goddamn you! Get off!

655
02:01:59.069 --> 02:02:00.195
Hmm.

656
02:02:12.124 --> 02:02:13.459
You Jerry-banging. Limburg-smelling...

657
02:02:17.713 --> 02:02:20.007
As Stanley said to Livingstone.

658
02:02:20.090 --> 02:02:22.259
Lieutenant Aldo Raine. I presume?

659
02:02:23.177 --> 02:02:24.553
Hans Landa.

660
02:02:26.722 --> 02:02:29.099
You've had a nice long run. Aldo.

661
02:02:30.017 --> 02:02:32.853
Alas. you're now in the hands of the SS.

662
02:02:32.936 --> 02:02:34.480
My hands to be exact.

663
02:02:34.563 --> 02:02:38.275
And they've been waiting a long time 
to touch you.

664
02:02:42.154 --> 02:02:43.947
Caught you flinching.

665
02:02:48.160 --> 02:02:50.370
Touch me again. Kraut-burger.

666
02:03:06.220 --> 02:03:07.221
Utivich?

667
02:03:07.304 --> 02:03:08.722
Is that you. Lieutenant?

668
02:03:08.806 --> 02:03:09.890
Yeah.

669
02:03:10.474 --> 02:03:12.559
Do you know what happened to Donny?

670
02:03:12.643 --> 02:03:13.769
Omar?

671
02:03:14.478 --> 02:03:15.479
The woman?

672
02:03:15.562 --> 02:03:16.814
No. I do not.

673
02:04:03.360 --> 02:04:06.905
Tell me. Aldo. 
if I were sitting where you're sitting.

674
02:04:06.989 --> 02:04:08.949
would you show me mercy?

675
02:04:13.537 --> 02:04:14.663
Nope.

676
02:04:15.330 --> 02:04:18.584
What is that English expression 
about shoes and feet?

677
02:04:18.667 --> 02:04:22.212
"Looks like the shoe is on the other foot." 
Yeah. I was just thinking that.

678
02:04:35.267 --> 02:04:38.145
So you're Aldo the Apache.

679
02:04:39.271 --> 02:04:40.481
So you're The Jew Hunter.

680
02:04:40.564 --> 02:04:42.274
I'm a detective.

681
02:04:42.357 --> 02:04:44.234
A damn good detective.

682
02:04:44.568 --> 02:04:46.153
Finding people is my specialty.

683
02:04:46.236 --> 02:04:48.655
so naturally. 
I worked for the Nazis finding people.

684
02:04:48.739 --> 02:04:51.867
And. yes. some of them were Jews. 
But Jew Hunter?

685
02:04:53.202 --> 02:04:55.078
Just a name that stuck.

686
02:04:55.537 --> 02:04:58.332
Well. you do have to admit. 
it is catchy.

687
02:04:59.792 --> 02:05:02.961
Do you control the nicknames
your enemies bestow on you?

688
02:05:03.045 --> 02:05:05.547
Aldo the Apache and the Little Man?

689
02:05:06.632 --> 02:05:08.759
What do you mean the Little Man?

690
02:05:08.842 --> 02:05:10.636
Germans' nickname for you.

691
02:05:10.719 --> 02:05:13.764
The Germans' nickname for me
is the Little Man?

692
02:05:14.139 --> 02:05:18.685
And as if to make my point. I'm a little surprised 
how tall you are in real life.

693
02:05:18.769 --> 02:05:21.188
I mean. you're a little fellow.
but not circus-midget little.

694
02:05:21.271 --> 02:05:23.065
as your reputation would suggest.

695
02:05:23.148 --> 02:05:24.691
Where's my men?

696
02:05:25.234 --> 02:05:27.569
Where's Bridget von Hammersmark?

697
02:05:30.447 --> 02:05:33.617
Well. let's just say.
she got what she deserved.

698
02:05:36.120 --> 02:05:38.622
And when you purchase friends
like Bridget von Hammersmark.

699
02:05:38.705 --> 02:05:40.707
you get what you pay for.

700
02:05:42.126 --> 02:05:47.131
Now as far as your paesanos.
Sergeant Donowitz and Private Omar...

701
02:05:47.214 --> 02:05:49.133
How you know our names?

702
02:05:49.716 --> 02:05:51.301
Lieutenant Aldo...

703
02:05:53.178 --> 02:05:54.596
if you don't think 
I wouldn't interrogate

704
02:05:54.680 --> 02:05:58.058
every single one of your
swastika-marked survivors...

705
02:06:00.477 --> 02:06:04.064
we simply aren't operating 
on the level of mutual respect I assumed.

706
02:06:04.148 --> 02:06:05.732
No. I guess not.

707
02:06:05.941 --> 02:06:11.071
Well. back to the whereabouts
of your two Italian saboteurs.

708
02:06:14.241 --> 02:06:15.993
As of this moment.

709
02:06:16.076 --> 02:06:20.914
both Omar and Donowitz should be sitting
in the very seats we left them in.

710
02:06:21.540 --> 02:06:25.169
Double-zero 23 and double-zero 24. 
if my memory serves.

711
02:06:25.919 --> 02:06:29.339
Explosives still around their ankles. 
still ready to explode.

712
02:06:29.423 --> 02:06:32.676
And your mission. 
some would call a terrorist plot.

713
02:06:32.759 --> 02:06:35.262
as of this moment. is still a go.

714
02:06:35.345 --> 02:06:38.682
That's a pretty exciting story.
What's next? Eliza on Ice?

715
02:06:38.765 --> 02:06:40.017
However...

716
02:06:41.894 --> 02:06:45.022
all I have to do is pick up
this phone right here.

717
02:06:45.105 --> 02:06:47.941
inform the cinema.
and your plan is kaput.

718
02:06:50.360 --> 02:06:55.574
If they're still there. and if they're still alive. 
and that's one big if...

719
02:06:56.909 --> 02:06:58.702
there ain't no way 
you're going to take them boys

720
02:06:58.786 --> 02:07:00.412
without setting off them bombs.

721
02:07:00.496 --> 02:07:02.247
I have no doubt.

722
02:07:02.331 --> 02:07:05.626
And. yes. some Germans will die.
Yes. it will ruin the evening.

723
02:07:05.709 --> 02:07:08.629
And. yes. Goebbels will be
very. very. very mad at you

724
02:07:08.712 --> 02:07:10.798
for what you've done to his big night.

725
02:07:12.049 --> 02:07:14.343
But you won't get Hitler.
you won't get Goebbels.

726
02:07:14.426 --> 02:07:17.471
you won't get Goring.
and you won't get Bormann.

727
02:07:17.554 --> 02:07:20.140
And you need all four to end the war.

728
02:07:21.809 --> 02:07:24.978
But if I don't pick up
this phone right here.

729
02:07:25.062 --> 02:07:27.397
you may very well get all four.

730
02:07:28.649 --> 02:07:33.487
And if you get all four.
you end the war...

731
02:07:34.738 --> 02:07:35.989
tonight.

732
02:07:37.366 --> 02:07:38.909
So. gentlemen...

733
02:07:39.618 --> 02:07:42.830
let's discuss the prospect
of ending the war tonight.

734
02:07:45.749 --> 02:07:47.584
So. the way I see it.

735
02:07:47.668 --> 02:07:51.880
since Hitler's death or possible rescue 
rests solely on my reaction...

736
02:07:52.548 --> 02:07:54.133
if I do nothing...

737
02:07:54.550 --> 02:07:57.261
it's as if I'm causing his death 
even more than yourselves.

738
02:07:57.344 --> 02:07:58.595
Wouldn't you agree?

739
02:07:59.263 --> 02:08:00.597
I guess so.

740
02:08:03.183 --> 02:08:05.185
How about you. Utivich?

741
02:08:05.269 --> 02:08:06.895
I guess so. too.

742
02:08:12.442 --> 02:08:13.694
Gentlemen. I have no intention

743
02:08:13.777 --> 02:08:16.864
of killing Hitler and killing Goebbels 
and killing Goring and killing Bormann.

744
02:08:16.947 --> 02:08:19.700
not to mention winning the war
single-handedly for the Allies.

745
02:08:19.783 --> 02:08:23.537
only later to find myself standing
before a Jewish tribunal.

746
02:08:25.622 --> 02:08:29.168
If you want to win the war tonight...

747
02:08:30.794 --> 02:08:32.963
we have to make a deal.

748
02:08:35.966 --> 02:08:37.718
What kind of deal?

749
02:08:37.801 --> 02:08:40.345
The kind you wouldn't
have the authority to make.

750
02:08:40.429 --> 02:08:44.975
However. I'm sure this mission of yours 
has a commanding officer.

751
02:08:45.976 --> 02:08:47.311
A general.

752
02:08:47.978 --> 02:08:49.646
I'm betting for...

753
02:08:51.356 --> 02:08:53.275
OSS would be my guess.

754
02:08:57.196 --> 02:08:59.656
That's a bingo!

755
02:09:02.659 --> 02:09:05.162
Is that the way you say it?
"That's a bingo."

756
02:09:05.245 --> 02:09:07.122
You just say. "Bingo."

757
02:09:07.206 --> 02:09:09.458
Bingo! How fun.

758
02:09:11.877 --> 02:09:14.963
But I digress. Where were we?
Yeah! Make a deal.

759
02:09:15.506 --> 02:09:19.927
Over there is a very capable two-way radio 
and sitting behind it

760
02:09:20.010 --> 02:09:24.181
is a more than capable radio operator 
named Hermann.

761
02:09:24.515 --> 02:09:26.850
Get me someone on the other end
of that radio

762
02:09:26.934 --> 02:09:29.978
with the power of the pen to authorize my...

763
02:09:30.062 --> 02:09:32.981
let's call it. 
the terms of my conditional surrender.

764
02:09:33.065 --> 02:09:35.484
If that tastes better going down.

765
02:09:36.276 --> 02:09:37.528
You know. where I'm from...

766
02:09:37.611 --> 02:09:39.488
Yeah?
Where is that exactly?

767
02:09:39.571 --> 02:09:41.615
Maynardville. Tennessee.

768
02:09:41.698 --> 02:09:44.159
I've done my share of bootlegging.

769
02:09:44.368 --> 02:09:48.038
Up there. if you engage in what 
the federal government calls illegal activity.

770
02:09:48.122 --> 02:09:50.249
but what we call just a man 
trying to make a living for his family

771
02:09:50.332 --> 02:09:54.753
selling moonshine liquor. 
it behooves oneself to keep his wits.

772
02:09:56.713 --> 02:10:00.134
Long story short. we hear a story
too good to be true...

773
02:10:00.801 --> 02:10:02.052
it ain't.

774
02:10:03.887 --> 02:10:06.640
Sitting in your chair. 
I would probably say the same thing.

775
02:10:06.723 --> 02:10:11.436
and 999.999 times out of a million.
you would be correct.

776
02:10:13.438 --> 02:10:17.025
But in the pages of history.
every once in a while.

777
02:10:17.609 --> 02:10:20.988
fate reaches out and extends its hand.

778
02:10:27.828 --> 02:10:29.788
What shall the history books read?

779
02:10:56.648 --> 02:10:59.860
<i>I implore you.
We must destroy that tower.</i>

780
02:11:01.278 --> 02:11:02.905
<i>Sarge. that tower...</i>

781
02:11:22.466 --> 02:11:24.384
<i>The tower stands!</i>

782
02:11:31.517 --> 02:11:34.019
Psst! Psst!

783
02:14:04.128 --> 02:14:06.296
So when the military history
of this night is written.

784
02:14:06.380 --> 02:14:10.050
it will be recorded 
that I was part of Operation Kino

785
02:14:10.134 --> 02:14:12.928
from the very beginning 
as a double agent.

786
02:14:13.011 --> 02:14:17.057
Anything I've done in my guise
as an SS Colonel

787
02:14:17.141 --> 02:14:20.185
was sanctioned by the OSS
as a necessary evil

788
02:14:20.269 --> 02:14:22.980
to establish my cover with the Germans.

789
02:14:23.188 --> 02:14:26.483
And it was my placement of 
Lieutenant Raine's dynamite

790
02:14:26.567 --> 02:14:29.528
in Hitler and Goebbels' opera box 
that assured their demise.

791
02:14:46.670 --> 02:14:49.673
By the way. 
that last part is actually true.

792
02:14:49.756 --> 02:14:54.678
I want my full military pension 
and benefits under my proper rank.

793
02:14:55.012 --> 02:14:57.431
I want to receive the 
Congressional Medal of Honor

794
02:14:57.514 --> 02:15:01.477
for my invaluable assistance 
in the toppling of the Third Reich.

795
02:15:02.895 --> 02:15:05.981
In fact. I want all the members 
of Operation Kino

796
02:15:06.064 --> 02:15:09.026
to receive the
Congressional Medal of Honor.

797
02:15:09.401 --> 02:15:13.113
Full citizenship for myself.
Well. that goes without saying.

798
02:15:13.405 --> 02:15:16.617
And I would like the 
United States of America

799
02:15:16.700 --> 02:15:20.788
to purchase property for me
on Nantucket Island

800
02:15:20.871 --> 02:15:24.124
as a reward for all the 
countless lives I've saved

801
02:15:24.208 --> 02:15:26.543
by bringing the tyranny
of the National Socialist Party

802
02:15:26.627 --> 02:15:30.255
to a swifter-than-imagined end.
Do you have all that. sir?

803
02:15:32.049 --> 02:15:35.511
I look forward to seeing you
face to face as well. sir.

804
02:15:36.386 --> 02:15:38.597
Lieutenant Raine?
Right here. 

805
02:15:41.809 --> 02:15:43.018
Yes. sir.

806
02:15:43.101 --> 02:15:46.855
<i>Colonel Landa will put you and Private Utivich 
in a truck as prisoners.</i>

807
02:15:46.939 --> 02:15:51.318
<i>Then he and his radio operator 
will get in the truck and drive to our lines.</i>

808
02:15:51.401 --> 02:15:55.989
<i>Upon crossing our lines. 
Colonel Landa and his man will surrender to you.</i>

809
02:15:56.073 --> 02:15:58.617
<i>You will then take over
driving of the truck</i>

810
02:15:58.700 --> 02:16:02.079
<i>and bring them straight to me for debriefing. 
Is that clear. Lieutenant?</i> 

811
02:16:02.162 --> 02:16:03.288
Yes. sir.

812
02:16:03.372 --> 02:16:04.832
<i>Over and out.</i>

813
02:21:49.009 --> 02:21:51.595
When I kill that guy.
you got 30 feet to get to that guard.

814
02:21:51.678 --> 02:21:53.639
- Can you do it?
- I have to. 

815
02:22:23.877 --> 02:22:25.212
Champagne?

816
02:23:17.055 --> 02:23:19.766
<i>Who wants to send a message to Germany?</i>

817
02:23:20.601 --> 02:23:22.936
<i>I have a message for Germany.</i>

818
02:23:26.398 --> 02:23:28.650
<i>That you are all going to die.</i>

819
02:23:32.404 --> 02:23:37.826
<i>And I want you to look deep into the face 
of the Jew who's going to do it!</i>

820
02:23:39.912 --> 02:23:42.998
<i>Marcel. burn it down.</i>

821
02:23:43.999 --> 02:23:45.501
Oui. Shosanna.

822
02:24:20.953 --> 02:24:23.080
<i>My name is Shosanna Dreyfus...</i>

823
02:24:23.455 --> 02:24:25.040
<i>and this is the face...</i>

824
02:24:27.000 --> 02:24:29.336
<i>of Jewish vengeance.</i>

825
02:26:35.003 --> 02:26:36.797
Hermann. uncuff them.

826
02:26:55.441 --> 02:26:59.445
I'm officially surrendering myself 
over to you. Lieutenant Raine.

827
02:27:00.571 --> 02:27:02.364
We're your prisoners.

828
02:27:03.198 --> 02:27:04.908
How about my knife?

829
02:27:10.873 --> 02:27:12.833
Thank you very much. Colonel.

830
02:27:12.916 --> 02:27:16.003
Utivich. cuff the Colonel's hands
behind his back.

831
02:27:16.086 --> 02:27:18.297
Is that really necessary?

832
02:27:18.380 --> 02:27:20.466
I'm a slave to appearances.

833
02:27:23.635 --> 02:27:25.137
Scalp Hermann.

834
02:27:26.805 --> 02:27:28.474
Are you mad?

835
02:27:28.849 --> 02:27:30.601
What have you done?

836
02:27:31.101 --> 02:27:34.438
I made a deal with your general
for that man's life!

837
02:27:35.522 --> 02:27:38.901
Yeah. they made that deal. But they don't
give a fuck about him. They need you.

838
02:27:38.984 --> 02:27:40.944
You'll be shot for this!

839
02:27:41.612 --> 02:27:45.115
Nah. I don't think so. More like chewed out.
I've been chewed out before.

840
02:27:46.450 --> 02:27:50.621
You know. Utivich and myself heard 
that deal you made with the brass.

841
02:27:51.079 --> 02:27:52.831
End the war tonight?

842
02:27:54.249 --> 02:27:55.793
I'd make that deal.

843
02:27:55.876 --> 02:27:57.711
How about you. Utivich?
You make that deal?

844
02:27:57.795 --> 02:27:58.796
I'd make that deal.

845
02:27:58.879 --> 02:28:01.381
I don't blame you.
Damn good deal.

846
02:28:02.132 --> 02:28:05.260
And that pretty little nest
you feathered for yourself.

847
02:28:05.344 --> 02:28:08.722
Well. if you're willing to barbecue
the whole High Command.

848
02:28:08.806 --> 02:28:11.809
I suppose that's worth
certain considerations.

849
02:28:12.559 --> 02:28:14.645
But I do have one question.

850
02:28:15.729 --> 02:28:18.482
When you get to your little place
on Nantucket Island.

851
02:28:18.565 --> 02:28:23.112
I imagine you won't take off 
that handsome-looking SS uniform of yours.

852
02:28:23.195 --> 02:28:24.530
Ain't you?

853
02:28:28.492 --> 02:28:30.369
That's what I thought.

854
02:28:31.120 --> 02:28:32.996
Now. that I can't abide.

855
02:28:34.414 --> 02:28:36.708
How about you. Utivich.
can you abide it?

856
02:28:36.792 --> 02:28:38.669
Not one damn bit. sir.

857
02:28:40.295 --> 02:28:42.381
I mean. if I had my way.

858
02:28:42.881 --> 02:28:47.344
you'd wear that goddamn uniform 
for the rest of your pecker-sucking life.

859
02:28:48.846 --> 02:28:49.847
But I'm aware that ain't practical.

860
02:28:49.930 --> 02:28:52.975
I mean. at some point. 
you're going to have to take it off.

861
02:28:53.058 --> 02:28:54.184
So...

862
02:28:55.144 --> 02:28:58.856
I'm going to give you a little something 
you can't take off.

863
02:29:23.797 --> 02:29:25.924
You know something. Utivich?

864
02:29:26.300 --> 02:29:29.094
I think this just might be my masterpiece.

865
02:29:30.305 --> 02:30:30.572
